NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000111 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000112 "=head1 NAME"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000113 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000114 "Tie::Handle::Offset - Tied handle that hides the beginning of a file"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000115 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000116 "=head1 VERSION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000117 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000118 "version 0.004"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000119 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000120 "=head1 SYNOPSIS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000121 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000122 "  use Tie::Handle::Offset;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000123 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000124 "  tie *FH, 'Tie::Handle::Offset', \"<\", $filename, { offset => 20 };"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000125 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000126 "=head1 DESCRIPTION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000127 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000128 "This modules provides a file handle that hides the beginning of a file."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000129 "After opening, the file is positioned at the offset location. C<seek()> and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000130 "C<tell()> calls are modified to preserve the offset."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000131 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000132 "For example, C<tell($fh)> will return 0, though the actual file position"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000133 "is at the offset.  Likewise, C<seek($fh,80,0)> will seek to 80 bytes from"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000134 "the offset instead of 80 bytes from the actual start of the file."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000135 ""
